  "finding": "Swift's completed implement-slice comparison improved recorded discovery quality from 2/4 to 4/4 and aggregate quality from 12/14 to 14/14. Both control arms were already 10/10, leaving no room for a control-partition gain under the predeclared criterion, so the raw state remains `no-improvement` with recommendation `keep A`. A corrected independent probe of the actual Swift workspace-after confirmed a separate valid array-backed-store contract gap: reference checks passed 15/15, outputs 1-A and 2-B passed 15/15 each, and outputs 1-B and 2-A failed 15/15 each with array rejection. This is tracked in [#146](https://github.com/ivo-toby/tiny-sdd/issues/146). This narrow discovery improvement does not establish broad transfer; the public disposition is inconclusive with the baseline retained pending strict-control qualification.",
  "reviewDisposition": {
    "state": "inconclusive",
    "recommendation": "gather-more",
    "reason": "Operator-supplied conservative publication disposition; raw experimental state remains preserved.",
    "followUp": "Retain the baseline; extend and version oracle coverage under [#146](https://github.com/ivo-toby/tiny-sdd/issues/146) and collect fresh independent control comparisons under [#126](https://github.com/ivo-toby/tiny-sdd/issues/126) before making a broad transfer recommendation."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Exploratory comparison: the primary analyst had prior control-source exposure; no blinded or untouched transfer claim is made.",
    "The measured discovery benefit is narrow and does not establish general model behavior; repeated paired runs are correlated and the control partition reached a ceiling.",
    "A corrected independent probe of the actual Swift workspace-after found the valid array-backed-store contract gap tracked in #146: reference checks passed 15/15, outputs 1-A and 2-B passed 15/15 each, and outputs 1-B and 2-A failed 15/15 each with array rejection. The digest-bound retained result is `local-research-root:swift-array-store-posthoc-probe-v3-results.json` (sha256 `b5098fc192d588ee3c6641a6674340cfe2c55c4c851637f7af0652708a69b3be`). This is a contract and finite oracle-coverage limitation, not a model-effectiveness result.",
    "Backend version, server enforcement and integration transfer remain UNKNOWN.",
    "The local SSH observer exited 255 at 13:40:35 before remote completion at 2026-10-19T13:43:55.031Z; remote execution completed independently, relay stop was recorded at 2026-10-19T13:43:56.541Z, and later read-only collection recovered all 28 cases, the report and relay-stop artifacts. No rerun was performed.",
    "An earlier posthoc v1 probe was excluded from model evidence after identity review found it used seeded benchmark candidates rather than the retained Swift workspace-after; its raw artifacts remain preserved separately. A v2 probe pack was refused before checks during metadata validation, so it also contributed no model evidence.",
